[h1]Phobos Auto Nav[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.34.1
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - development candidate

Give Polaris the long approach while you keep an eye on the ship. Asterel boards plug into the Polaris navigation station and fly, dock, pursue and aim using the ship's own thrusters, torch, sensors and weapons.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Phobos' Asterel N1 Polaris Auto Nav Module:[/b] fly to a tracked ship, station or asteroid and stop at your chosen distance, or Dock and Approach & Dock. Asteroids within 1,000 km, Fly only, stopping inside tether reach.
[*][b]Phobos' Asterel N2 Polaris Pursuit Module:[/b] everything the N1 does, plus Rendezvous to match a target's motion once, or Follow to keep pace.
[*][b]Phobos' Asterel N3 Polaris Fire Control System:[/b] choose weapons, volleys and RCS aiming. Select a fire target and lift the cover to Engage. Cease Fire stops firing and aiming; Return to ship controls can allow automatic fire again.
[*]With N2 and N3 fitted, Combat on Track matches range and keeps weapons facing the fire target.
[*]Torch burns run the reactor the way the game's own course plot does, under the console's torch safety limit. Auto Nav never ignites, repairs or refuels the reactor.
[*]If the target or a nearby hazard is too faint, Auto Nav switches on the fewest sensors that fix it, non-emitting first, and tells you in the crew log and on the nav map. It switches off only its own sensors; your switches always win. Choose All, Passive or Off in Sensors > AutoEngage.
[*]Local avoidance steers around tracked contacts and asteroid-field rocks. Undock & Depart checks crew, clearance and connections, then opens at least a 1 km gap. Ordinary Fly never undocks.
[*]Flights, fire control and Combat support one securely braced tow in free space.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[list]
[*]Buy boards new at regional supply kiosks, used at the K-Leg fixer, broken at the K-Leg supply kiosk or refurbished at the Venus and Flotilla scrap kiosks. CCRE and GalCon faction kiosks sell them for scrip: the N1 at Warm standing, the N2 and N3 at Friendly. You can also build one at an installed Bar or Dining Table from the game's Polaris course plot modules, or find one in module salvage. Broken boards need Repair.
[*]Fit the board into a module slot of the Polaris navigation station; it has no floor INSTALL tile. Open the Phobos flight hub on the station, select a target your sensors track, set arrival preferences and choose Fly, Dock or Approach & Dock.
[*]Disengage releases the controls. The throttle slider sets how hard Auto Nav may use RCS.
[*]In the F3 console, phobosnav status reports the current flight.
[*]Board prices, repair bills, offers and salvage odds are a readable file in the framework folder; override it in BepInEx/config/PhobosAutoNav.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.123.0 or newer.
[*]BepInEx 5 through EddieSM / EsMM27's [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3741030124]BepInEx Mod Loader[/url], including its one-time setup.
[*]Disable the original Auto Navigate before engaging Phobos Auto Nav. It is not a dependency, and installing ours does not disable it.
[/list]

[h2]Installing from the Workshop[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to the BepInEx Mod Loader and follow its setup instructions.
[*]Subscribe to Phobos Auto Nav and the Phobos items listed under Required items.
[*]Start Ostranauts once so the loader copies the plugins, then restart it once so they load. Do the same after each update.
[*]Check that the mods are enabled in the MODS screen.
[*]Used the repository's local installer before? Remove those local copies first so only one copy loads. See the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/installing-mods.md]installation guide[/url].
[/list]

[h2]Saves and limits[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Disengage and Stop are not a brake.[/b] They remove thrust and the ship keeps coasting. Leave braking room.
[*]No guaranteed collision-free flight, successful hit or intact capture. Losing track of the target or a hazard releases thrust and waits for Resume. A one-off failure in the game's own ship update is ridden out; repeated failures suspend the flight for Resume.
[*]Docking needs clearance and the docking console open for the final clamp. Departure and pursuit pause after loading, docking carries on, and Combat never restarts on reload.
[*]Ordinary saves are supported; saved flights keep their settings. Since 0.28.0 flight progress settles every two real seconds and before every save. Keep required mods installed while a save uses their content. Updating does not refill existing shops or old loot containers.
[*]Automated checks pass; in-game checks of torch and station-cluster approaches are still in progress.
[/list]

[h2]Credits and sources[/h2]
Created by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko). Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games, Kitfox Games or the research institutions cited below. Research informs design; operating limits remain gameplay choices.
Guidance and target tracking adapt [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3745533691]Auto Navigate by Gravy / mrkmg[/url]. That upstream-derived code is credited to its author and excluded from the MIT grant; no explicit reuse licence was found. See the third-party notices.
Sensing and guidance research, not validation of this controller: NASA Goddard's Raven, Zhou at NASA Langley (2012), ESA's LIRIS experiment (Airbus, Jena Optronik and Sodern), Hartley, Trodden, Richards and Maciejowski in ESA's ORCSAT project (2012) and ESA ATV operations. Daniel Fedor of Blue Bottle Games supplies the combat context. The departure, pursuit and fire-control guides link each source beside its claim.
Original artwork uses AI-assisted production; provenance and licensing are recorded separately.

